> If ek-d3sys-pm is to be believed (and it's the bible by which I did
> the port to begin with 8-), then, as i mentioned to you earlier:
>
> page 9-13: "The ISDN registers, like the SCC registers, are
> longword-aligned; data is read from and written to byte 1."

There is a hint why some IOASIC devices registers appear on strange
location at "Figure 9 IOCTL Subsystem" on page 7-1.  The document
mentions IOCTL ASIC has 16bit bus.  The figure depicts AM79C30A and
a pair of Z85C30s are wired with "IOBUS,HI" upper half of 16bit bus,
while DS1287A and two of ROMs are wired with "IOBUS,LO" lower half.

