*** I had a reply from Toru Nishimura with a pointer to a 3000/700 1.5
snapshot WSCONS kernel which can *only* use the PMAGB-B framebuffer. If
you have any other TC frambuffer - you are out of luck (for the moment). I
have been able to netboot and run my 3000/700 diskless using this kernel.
A "release" version of the WSCONS kernel for the 3000/700 (and friends) is
at least 6 months away.

After unpacking the sets and configuring the system (all done manually
whilst running diskless), I then booted off the local disk using the
standard 1.4.2 kernel. It still goes to the serial console but I don't
care as I can now access the machine over the network.

