> 3000/700 or am I doomed to failure w/o a MMJ cable?

*** I am yet to try to compile a kernel with WSCONS support. However, I
did have problems using the first 1.5 snapshot kernel on the console
*after* going multiuser. Single user mode works without a hitch.

> 3. Where can I get a (cheap :-) MMJ cable (I'm not a hardware person) -

*** RS Components make a 6-lead MMJ-MMJ cable and MMJ-D25 and MMJ-D9
converters. A 3m MMj-MMJ cable with both the MMJ-D25 and MMJ-D9 converters
costs around 16 pounds (incl delivery)... Not cheap (but available).

Relevant RS part numbers are:

1. 6-lead MMJ patch cord grey - 446-670
2. MMJ-D9 socket adaptor      - 486-331
3. MMJ-D25 socket adaptor     - 486-353

HTH,

--Nino

